    "jays": {
      "full_name": "Toronto Blue Jays",
      "league": "MLB",
      "record": "16-21",
      "detail": "4th in AL East",
      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "Shane McClanahan carved up the Blue Jays like a Thanksgiving turkey - 16 2/3 scoreless innings now, his third straight gem - as Toronto mustered four hits and <strong>dropped a 3-0 shutout to the Rays on Wednesday, completing a brutal three-game sweep</strong> at Tropicana Field. That's four straight losses, the last three a 0-12 skid against Tampa's staff, plunging the defending AL champs to 16-21 and fourth in the East, 9 games back with a playoff seed of 12. The bats vanished - Vladimir Guerrero Jr. went 0-for-4 in the finale, silent in a lineup that's lost five of seven and eight of its last nine at the Trop, where the ghosts of Hurricane Milton repairs seem to haunt more than just the stands. This isn't a blip; it's a nosedive for a club that arrived with pennant buzz and now stares at irrelevance. The pitching held some ground early, but the offense evaporated under the dome's dim lights. Buckle up - <strong>Friday's home tilt against the Angels at 6:07 PM ET offers a lifeline, but without sparks from Vlad or the lumber, this slump devours the season</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated May 7, 2026"
      },
