      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Commanders",
        "body": "The Washington Commanders emerged from the 2026 NFL Draft smoke not as saviors, but as a squad finally flexing defensive muscle after a <strong>5-12 slog that left them third in the NFC East, six games back</strong> - a grim reminder of last year's pass-funnel nightmare. <strong>Snagging Ohio State linebacker Sonny Styles at No. 7 overall</strong> injects the versatility this unit has craved, a chess-piece hybrid who can blitz, cover slots, and set edges in ways that Kliff Kingsbury's departed offense never demanded. With David Blough now calling plays, Styles slots into a revamped front seven, potentially shoving veterans aside for immediate snaps - think 400-plus college tackles translating to rookie heat on quarterbacks. Undrafted free agents remain a quiet scramble, but the real juice is cap space dangling a cornerback splash before camp. No more excuses in D.C.; this rookie class screams scheme fit under new blood. <strong>Watch free agency next week - will they land that shutdown DB, or limp into September exposed again?</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated May 7, 2026"
      },
